  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Twenty-one selected short, philosophical performance pieces by Thomas McEvilley composed from the lore surrounding Diogenes of Sinope. As the plates are loose and unpaginated, they can be read in a random order"--"Peter Koch, Printers" web site.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Letterpress edition, a facsimile of the engraved lead-tablet edition of the same year. Includes at front an essay by McEvilley, Diogenes of Sinope : selected performance pieces, adapted from his article in Artforum magazine (March 1983).</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Title in brown and black; title vignette.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Lettering by Christopher Stinehour"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Printed by Peter Rutledge Koch, assisted by Richard Seibert. Housed in a cardboard box with illustrated cover printed in brown and black.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">LC copy is one of 500 copies from the 1st printing. Accompanied by a "variant keepsake and prototype before cardboard box," a loose set of the 11 printed leaves of chipboard. In a manilla envelope, 18 x 12 cm., printed (upside down) with the text of one of the performance pieces: Diogenes sat in the public square one afternoon glueing shut the pages of a book.</subfield>
    <subfield code="5">DLC</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="504" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
